Z||000000||Brucepts||06-05-2001||01:01 AM||||Ok here is my question, has anyone had problems with the dash lights going dead? I have one light the left side tach light (84 SE) that has just gone dead. No power to the light via the circuit board. I checked it with a volt meter and no volts on the circuit board. I swapped the light sockets from place to place and this had no effect either. Any ideas? Anyone else have this problem? Thanks in advance.<P>------------------<BR>Advanced Dealer in the Great Material Continuum . . .<BR>Non Fiero Website: <A HREF="http://tractorsport.com" TARGET=_blank>http://tractorsport.com</A> <BR>You can't race a dyno . . .||||reg||1
Z||000001||Indiana_resto_guy||06-05-2001||04:48 AM||||Which indicator would that bulb light?||||reg||1
Z||000002||Brucepts||06-05-2001||08:46 AM||||Appears to me like I said in my post that it is a side light for the tachometer. There is one on each side of the speedo, but only one lights on my tachometer which is on the passenger side of the insturment (right side) the left side one doesn't work. Nor does it appear to have power going through the circuit board to it.<P>------------------<BR>Advanced Dealer in the Great Material Continuum . . .<BR>Non Fiero Website: <A HREF="http://tractorsport.com" TARGET=_blank>http://tractorsport.com</A> <BR>You can't race a dyno . . .||||reg||1
Z||000003||84Bill||06-05-2001||10:08 AM||||Check the "plug" connector on both sides of the cluster. Give them a wiggle when the lights are on. Mine was doing the same thing about a week ago and I fixed the problem.<BR>Also you may just want to remove the plugs and check the contacts in the cluster since they can get all out of wack when the plug is removed and installed several times.||||reg||3
Z||000004||cadaver||06-05-2001||10:41 PM||||Yes if you have had it out. I installed my cluster and the foil on some of the contacts got folded. My dash did all kinds of weird things till I found it.||||reg||1
Z||000005||grinthock||06-05-2001||10:58 PM||||Had the same problem in my 85, contacts were pretty much toast, so I just soldered a wire from another socket to that socket||||reg||1
